Lucky Sevens video notes: all nine bottles rendered, layering mock exists

Notes-only change. The render work itself lives in the FCCN-ANTIBODY workspace
(not a repo), so this is the pointer that makes it findable from the video side.

- All nine welded pieces are rendered with `bin/render-bottle-loop.mjs` into
  `FCCN-ANTIBODY/renders/lucky-sevens/<slug>/` (frames + mp4 + gif + manifest).
  Every set self-decoded and passed the simulated-camera catch test.
- EliseAI (2 KB, K=25) failed the catch test at the default 1.5× overhead — with
  only ~38 distinct frames the fountain set didn't span all blocks, and looping
  the same frames can't fix that — so it was rendered at 2×. Worth a default
  floor in the renderer for tiny payloads; not done here.
- `mock.html` next to the renders layers the loops over a stand-in of the cover
  with the real audio, five placement options, and an editable cue sheet.

Deliberately not done: no cue times set (by ear is yours), no final-bake signing
(needs the DW identity), and the cover in the mock is the snide version because
your own is held back.
